      <div class="cp-faq-list">
        <details id="keyboard-limits">
          <summary>Can I disable my Mac keyboard for cleaning?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>Stillkeys captures typing while its foreground cleaning screen is active and disables Command-Tab for that session. It does not turn off your keyboard hardware or block every system shortcut.</p><p>Power, Touch ID, media keys, some system controls, and Command-Option-Escape remain available. Your mouse and trackpad continue to work.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I get back to my Mac?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>Click Finish cleaning with your mouse or trackpad, hold Escape continuously for two seconds, or let the timer finish. A brief Escape tap won’t stop your session.</p><p>Stillkeys also ends the session if it loses focus, your Mac goes to sleep, or your display setup changes.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which Macs does it work on?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>Stillkeys is built for Macs running macOS {{ stillkeys.minimumMacOS }} or later, with Apple silicon and Intel support. It follows your Mac’s light or dark appearance.</p><p>The Mac App Store version doesn’t need Accessibility permission, administrator access, or any extra setup.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details id="privacy-details">
          <summary>What information does the app collect?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>Stillkeys does not collect, store, or transmit personal information. It has no accounts, advertising, analytics, tracking, or third-party SDKs.</p><p>During a session, it discards keyboard events and checks whether Escape is held so you can exit. It doesn’t record typed text or keep a key history. The timer and your duration choice stay in memory and are cleared when you quit.</p><p>Optional support and cleaning-guide links open in your mail app or browser, which have their own privacy practices. macOS may handle diagnostics according to your system settings. This describes the Stillkeys app; see <a href="/privacy/">Coffee &amp; Fun’s website privacy policy</a> for this website.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Anything to know before cleaning?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>Always follow your device manufacturer’s cleaning instructions. Apple recommends shutting down and disconnecting power before cleaning. Stillkeys does not replace those steps or make liquid cleaning safe.</p><p><a href="https://support.apple.com/103258">Read Apple’s cleaning guidance <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is there a subscription?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="cp-answer"><p>No. {% if stillkeys.appStoreUrl %}Stillkeys is a {{ stillkeys.plannedPrice }} USD one-time purchase on the Mac App Store.{% else %}Stillkeys is coming to the Mac App Store with a planned one-time price of {{ stillkeys.plannedPrice }} USD.{% endif %} There are no subscriptions or in-app purchases. Local prices may vary.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
